# DTO & Mapper Pattern

## DTOs (`data/model/`)
```kotlin
@Serializable
data class {Feature}Dto(
    @SerialName("id") val id: Int,
    @SerialName("registration_number") val registrationNumber: String,
    @SerialName("created_at") val createdAt: String? = null
)
```
- `@Serializable` on every DTO
- `@SerialName("snake_case")` for every field (API uses snake_case)
- All fields nullable or with defaults for safe deserialization
- Nested DTOs for embedded objects (e.g., `AssignedDriverDto`)

## Request DTOs
```kotlin
@Serializable
data class Create{Feature}Request(
    @SerialName("field_name") val fieldName: String
)
```

## Mappers (`data/mapper/`)
```kotlin
@Inject
class {Feature}Mapper {
    fun mapToDomain(dto: {Feature}Dto): {Feature} { ... }
    fun mapToDomainList(dtos: List<{Feature}Dto>): List<{Feature}> = dtos.map { mapToDomain(it) }
    fun mapToRequest(entity: {Feature}): Create{Feature}Request { ... }
}
```
- `@Inject` on mapper class
- `mapToDomain` converts DTO → domain entity
- `mapToRequest` converts domain entity → request DTO
- Date normalization via `FleetDateTime` in mapper
- ID conversion: API `Int` → domain `String` via `toString()`
